        </div>
        <div class="why">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Why us</span>
            <h2 data-split>Why hire one team instead of <em>five suppliers?</em></h2>
            <p class="reveal">When ads, social, email and outreach sit with different suppliers, nobody owns the number that matters. Each reports a metric that looks good on its own, and the leaks between channels stay hidden. One team running the whole path sees those leaks and fixes them first.</p>
            <div class="btns reveal"><a class="btn" href="/contact/"><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>Talk to us about your goals</a></div>
          </div>
          <ul class="approach">
            <li class="reveal"><img src="/img/3d/diagnose.webp" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>Revenue is the scoreboard</h3><p>Every channel is judged by cost per customer and sales. Clicks and likes are inputs, not results.</p></div></li>
            <li class="reveal d1"><img src="/img/3d/funnel.webp" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>One plan across channels</h3><p>Ads, content and outreach point at the same buyers, and the follow-up is built before the traffic arrives.</p></div></li>
            <li class="reveal d2"><img src="/img/3d/content.webp" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>Creative made in-house</h3><p>Video, design and copy are produced by the same team that runs the campaigns, so tests never wait.</p></div></li>
            <li class="reveal d3"><img src="/img/3d/ai.webp" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>Automation does the busywork</h3><p>AI agents handle research, sorting and reporting. People handle strategy, creative and judgment.</p></div></li>
            <li class="reveal"><img src="/img/3d/shield.webp" alt="" width="64" height="64" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>You own every account</h3><p>Ad accounts, domains, mailboxes and data are in your name. If we part ways, everything keeps running.</p></div></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10. Pinned process stepper -->
